  "notes": "No bot check was hit. Images were not downloaded or viewed, so choices rest on file names and where the photos sit on the pages. Logo is the site's header logo (SVG); the white version in the footer was not used. Hero is the slide 'Hervey Bay - one of the world's BEST Whale Watching destinations' on the home page (a 1920 pixel wide crop, shown with the site's own text laid over it in code); a person should check it, and the first home slide (rotator-images/o0gplg/3-vz03v2l6.jpg) is the alternative. Left out as banners or graphics with text or logos: the page banner for Whales & Lunch at K'Gari (a Canva 'Billboard' PNG), the home slide that is a Canva 'Billboard' PNG, the Aqua Oasis Cruise logo (AOC logo website.png), the 'Untitled design' PNGs and JPG, the BOQE award stamps, the Tripadvisor graphic, the Graphic1 PNG on the charter page and the 'testing-N' banner files. Left out as likely belonging to others: Kingfisher Bay Resort photos (file names 'Kingfisher Bay Resort- external', 'SBAREXT', 'kbr-4'), the K'Gari day tour photos on the Whales & K'Gari Trails page (file names 'fet2', 'fet12', '200', numbered '1-' to '5-' files and hash-named files, apparently Fraser Explorer Tours), and the hash-prefixed 'QCW' files (for example 'a749441a...QCW8_lg'). The unprefixed QCW10_lg, QCW11_lg and QCW13_lg files look like a supplied photo set with no credit on the site; they were left out so a person can decide. So the Whales & K'Gari Trails trip has no photos. Gallery leads with whale photos, then the boat and Aqua Oasis. Facebook-style and Instagram-style file names are on the operator's own site and are treated as its own posts. The Swim with the Whales page has its own set of nine photos; they are not used because the swim is an add-on and not a trip, and a person can add them if wanted. Videos: the first three are embedded on the operator's own pages (home, Afternoon Whale Watch, Swim with the Whales); the rest are from the YouTube channel the site links to (UC3zusfevb1ZVdD_LkmNt1TQ). The channel also lists a K'gari Ocean Safari video (about seven years old, a product not on the site now) and 'Whale spotting from aircraft', both left out."
}
